    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέορτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>newly arisen,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δ᾽ ἐστίν, ὦ παῖ Λαΐου, ν.
			αὖ</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1507
			</span></i>; of persons, <i>new,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ ν. ἅδε νύμφα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					894
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); also, <i>youthful</i> (expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφηβος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν ν. Ἑρμιόναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					872
				</span></i>
			 (lyr., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεοργόν</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ουργόν</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i>).</div>
